From 46442d370e356b649a6d56a9b4c41ebc9eaf368a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:00:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add parameter sensitivity analysis (Figs. 9-11)

Answers the reviewer question that the paper currently deflects: how much of
the ownership switch is the mechanism and how much is the particular numbers
in Appendix 5.1. Each free parameter is scaled (gains, precisions) or biased
(log-precisions) away from its published value while M1 and M2 stay exactly as
published, and the switch is detected again.

  switch_metrics  requires M1 to be the experienced hypothesis for the whole
                  visible period AND M2 to take over for at least 1 s after
                  covering, so an agent that was illusory from the start does
                  not count as having switched. The zero crossing is
                  interpolated so the switch time is not quantised to dt.
  Fig. 9          one parameter at a time, 10 noise realisations per point
  Fig. 10         all six perturbed at once, 300 random parameter sets
  Fig. 11         four parameters, four switches, for the appendix

Results: the switch survives x0.25-x2 of k_lam, x0.1-x100 of k_state,
x0.01-x10 of P_X, +/-4 of eta_lam, x0.01-x100 of P_lam(Av) and -4..+6 of
lam_covered(Av), and 298/300 joint perturbations. It has three limits, each
mechanistically interpretable: too fast a precision learner is illusory before
covering, too strong a prior on the Av precision prevents the switch (the
continuous version of Fig. 4), and too mild an occlusion never triggers it.

Figs. 2-8 are untouched, and simulate() is verified bit-identical across 24
configurations. P_X was hardcoded as eye(n) inside simulate and so could not
be swept; it is now p.P_X, defaulting to 1, which reproduces eye(n) exactly.
Structs without the field still run.

