From f631a7c30999f907287c6518d5450fc996f717d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:19:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Simplify Fig. 9 to four parameters against their own
 values

Fig. 9 now plots each parameter's own value on the x-axis instead of a
multiple of the published one, with a dashed line marking the value used in
the paper simulations; which values those are is stated in the figure's
description rather than on the axes.

  - four panels (k_lam, eta_lam, P_lam(Av), lam_covered(Av)) instead of six.
    k_state and P_X are dropped because they provably do nothing near their
    paper values: expm(K_X*H*dt) has already underflowed to zero, so the state
    update is the exact Newton step, and P_X = 1 is added to an M'*Pz*M whose
    entries are of order 1e3. Fig. 10 still perturbs all six.
  - one trial per point at the paper's noise realisation, plotted only where
    the switch occurs, so a curve that stops marks a value at which the
    illusion no longer arises
  - removed the across-seed ribbon and the bottom strip of markers
  - x-limits stop one grid step past the last switching point, so sweeps that
    deliberately run ten decades do not leave most of the axis blank
  - panel titles name the parameter's role, axes carry the symbol, ticks are
    set explicitly, y-labels only on the left column: nothing overlaps

Note the k_lam limit at ~11 that the ten-realisation version reported is not
visible in a single-trial figure -- above it M2 gets ahead before covering in
about half of the realisations, not all. This is recorded in the README.

Figs. 2-8 remain bit-identical across 24 configurations; Figs. 10 and 11 are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UfwYpwGVozHGhaYv68cWf3
