+Fig. 9 plots each parameter against its own value, with the dashed vertical
+line at the value used for the paper simulations. A point appears only where
+the switch actually occurs, so a curve that stops has reached a value at which
+the illusion no longer arises. One trial per point, at the paper's noise
+realisation. Fig. 11 adds a second row showing `U(M1) - U(M2)`, because the two
+uncertainty curves are only ~0.05 apart before covering and ~0.5 apart after
