From 2e3cd4cf186d7d79e0d4f9a030ef716320fd709f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:28:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Give Fig. 9 explicit axes positions so nothing overlaps

subplot(2,2,...) leaves too little room between the rows for x-labels that
carry superscripts and subscripts, so the top row's label touched the bottom
row's title. The four axes are now positioned by hand with roughly twice that
gap between rows, and the margins are sized for what sits outside the axes:
the y-label on the left, the centred titles above (a long one overflows to the
right of its own column), and the x-label subscripts, which hang lower than
the tick labels.

Also shortened the lam_covered panel title, which was long enough to run past
the right edge of the figure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UfwYpwGVozHGhaYv68cWf3
